================================================================================
1. ENVIRONMENT & ARCHITECTURE SETUP
================================================================================
[ ] Repository & Files: Initialize repository adhering to all mandatory folder and file naming constraints[cite: 1].
[ ] Environment Security: Store all API keys, database credentials, third-party secrets, and JWT keys in a .env file[cite: 1].
[ ] Git Hygiene: Ensure .env and sensitive credentials are added to .gitignore and excluded from Git history[cite: 1].
[ ] Docker Setup: Configure Docker Compose for Next.js frontend, NestJS backend, PostgreSQL database, and media/torrent storage.

================================================================================
2. USER INTERFACE & AUTHENTICATION (SECTION III.1)
================================================================================
[ ] Registration: Implement signup requiring email, username, first name, last name, and password[cite: 1].
[ ] Password Protection: Securely hash passwords (e.g., bcrypt/argon2) before DB storage; NEVER store plain text[cite: 1].
[ ] OmniAuth Strategy 1: Implement 42 OAuth authentication strategy[cite: 1].
[ ] OmniAuth Strategy 2: Implement a second OAuth strategy (e.g., GitHub or Google)[cite: 1].
[ ] Native Login & Logout: Enable username/password authentication and a 1-click logout button accessible from all pages[cite: 1].
[ ] Password Recovery: Send password reset links via email with secure reset tokens[cite: 1].
[ ] Profile Viewing: Allow users to view any profile (displaying picture and info, keeping email strictly private)[cite: 1].
[ ] Profile Editing: Allow authenticated users to edit their own email, info, and profile picture[cite: 1].
[ ] Localization: Support language preference selection, defaulting to English[cite: 1].
[ ] Layout & Mobile: Ensure standard site layout (header, main, footer) that is responsive on small mobile resolutions[cite: 1].

================================================================================
3. LIBRARY & MOVIE DISCOVERY (SECTION III.2)
================================================================================
[ ] Access Control: Restrict the library section exclusively to authenticated users[cite: 1].
[ ] Dual Source Search: Query at least two external video sources (e.g., OMDb, TMDb, YTS API)[cite: 1].
[ ] Default Library View: If no search query is entered, display popular videos sorted by criteria (e.g., seeds, downloads)[cite: 1].
[ ] Search Results: Display search results as thumbnails sorted by name[cite: 1].
[ ] Thumbnail Cards: Display title, production year, IMDb rating, and cover image on each thumbnail[cite: 1].
[ ] Watched Status: Visually distinguish between watched and unwatched videos on thumbnails[cite: 1].
[ ] Infinite Scroll: Load next page asynchronously upon scrolling (no manual page navigation links)[cite: 1].
[ ] Sorting & Filtering: Allow sorting and filtering by title, genre, IMDb score, production year, etc.[cite: 1]

================================================================================
4. VIDEO STREAMING & BACKGROUND ENGINE (SECTION III.3)
================================================================================
[ ] Details Page: Display video player, summary, cast/crew (director, main cast, producer), year, length, IMDb score, cover image, and prior comments[cite: 1].
[ ] Forbidden Libraries Rule: Ensure NO forbidden torrent streaming libraries are used (e.g., no webtorrent, pulsar, or peerflix)[cite: 1].
[ ] Background Downloading: Initiate background Torrent download on the server in a non-blocking manner[cite: 1].
[ ] On-The-Fly Streaming: Start streaming to the player via HTTP 206 Partial Content as soon as sufficient chunk data is buffered[cite: 1].
[ ] Dynamic Transcoding: Transcode non-browser-native formats (at minimum .mkv) on-the-fly into compatible formats (e.g., MP4/WebM)[cite: 1].
[ ] Subtitle Management: Automatically download and serve English subtitles, plus preferred language subtitles if video language differs[cite: 1].
[ ] Server Cleanup: Save fully downloaded movies on disk; purge movies unwatched for over 1 month via a background worker[cite: 1].

================================================================================
5. COMMENTS SYSTEM (SECTION III.3 & III.4)
================================================================================
[ ] Post Comments: Allow authenticated users to leave comments on video pages[cite: 1].
[ ] View Comments: Display a chronological list of prior comments under the video details[cite: 1].

================================================================================
6. MANDATORY RESTFUL API CONTRACT (SECTION III.4)
================================================================================
[ ] Authentication: Protect API routes with OAuth2 / Bearer Token authorization[cite: 1].
[ ] Route Lockout: Reject any unlisted API call and return the appropriate HTTP error code (e.g., 404 or 405)[cite: 1].

Expose the following exact endpoints:
[ ] POST /oauth/token
    - Expects client + secret (or username/password credentials)[cite: 1].
    - Returns an auth token[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /users
    - Returns list of users with id and username[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /users/:id
    - Returns username, email address, profile picture URL[cite: 1].
[ ] PATCH /users/:id
    - Accepts username, email, password, profile picture URL[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /movies
    - Returns frontpage movies list with id and name[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /movies/:id
    - Returns name, id, IMDb mark, production year, length, available subtitles, comment count[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /comments
    - Returns list of latest comments with author username, date, content, id[cite: 1].
[ ] GET /comments/:id
    - Returns comment content, author username, comment id, date posted[cite: 1].
[ ] PATCH /comments/:id
    - Accepts comment, username[cite: 1].
[ ] DELETE /comments/:id
    - Deletes target comment by ID[cite: 1].
[ ] POST /comments (OR POST /movies/:movie_id/comments)
    - Accepts comment, movie_id; server populates rest[cite: 1].

================================================================================
7. SECURITY & EVALUATION DEFENSE (CHAPTER V)
================================================================================
[ ] SQL Injection: Verify full protection against SQL injection across all queries[cite: 1].
[ ] XSS Prevention: Escape/sanitize user input across all forms, profile inputs, and comment fields[cite: 1].
[ ] Form Validation: Implement robust server-side and client-side input validation[cite: 1].
[ ] Console Hygiene: ZERO errors, warnings, or notices in server logs or browser developer console[cite: 1].
[ ] Defense Readiness: Prepare demonstration showing that the API is fully RESTful and matches all specs[cite: 1].





